only four years ago but it seems like a  lifetime away so much has changed in  British politics since of 2015 general  election  grexit has transformed the political  landscape bringing in new banners and  perhaps at this election new MPs - but  it's also strained our politics to a  breaking point and is pushing some  people away what's been surprising and  worrying is the number of women who  joined Parliament in this decade who are  deciding to call it a day in the prime  of their careers let me show you some of  them there's this woman Seema Kennedy 45  years old the former assistant to Teresa  may then there's a sovereign cabinet  minister Nicky Morgan just 47 years old  former Home Secretary amber rod former  government ministers Mims Davis and  Sarah Newton both deciding to quit  Parliament all together and then on the  Labour benches you've got Gloria de  Pierrot and you've got the former  conservative turned Lib Dem Heidi Allen  both women citing toxic levels of abuse  as a reason for quitting politics this  former Minister won't be standing either  another woman from the moderate wing of  the Conservatives on her way out the his  two colleagues you know what were you  surprised I was saw that Nicki Asafa  cabinet minister had decided to call it  quits I was really shocked and at that  moment um I thought I'm gonna fight on  I'm definitely gonna fight on too many  of us are going from our side of the  party to many good women are going and  that was you know the only last Thursday  so you know my decision was made just  after that really but out of step with  her local party over brexit Margate  James decided not to fight on she's not  even sure she can vote conservative  anymore were you very conservative in  the next election I would like to  reserve judgment to see who my  association selects to replace me I am  hopeful that I will be voting  conservative in Stourbridge as long as  they select somebody really decent she's  a victim of brexit warfare this is not  what others signed up for I don't think  that's that is what a lot of women want  their contribution to be you know just  on one-sided tribal aggressive form  forms of politics I don't think that's  necessary I don't think it's desirable  and I don't think it suits the majority  of women's style a hostile environment  that needs to change there's no need to  talk about politics in terms of war and  all of this it's just so unnecessary it  isn't a game  it's not a war and we need to dial all  that stuff down for all these MPs  tomorrow is their last day in this place  record numbers of women now sit on these  benches but many here not sure if that  will still be true on the other side of  this snap election bathra be Sky News  Westminster
 

